NNAAMMEE
     ssppaammllooggdd — spamd whitelist updating daemon

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     ssppaammllooggdd [--DDII] [--ii _i_n_t_e_r_f_a_c_e] [--ll _p_f_l_o_g___i_n_t_e_r_f_a_c_e] [--WW _w_h_i_t_e_e_x_p]
              [--YY _s_y_n_c_t_a_r_g_e_t]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     ssppaammllooggdd manipulates the spamd(8) database in _/_v_a_r_/_d_b_/_s_p_a_m_d used for
     greylisting.  ssppaammllooggdd updates the _/_v_a_r_/_d_b_/_s_p_a_m_d whitelist entries when‐
     ever a connection to port 25 is logged to the pflog(4) interface.  The
     source addresses of inbound connections are whitelisted when seen by
     ssppaammllooggdd to ensure that their entries in _/_v_a_r_/_d_b_/_s_p_a_m_d do not expire if
     the connecting host continues to send legitimate mail.  The destination
     addresses of outbound connections are whitelisted when seen by ssppaammllooggdd
     so that replies to outbound mail may be received without initial
     greylisting delays.  Greylisting is explained more fully in spamd(8).

     The options are as follows:

     --DD      Debugging mode.  ssppaammllooggdd does not disassociate from the control‐
             ling terminal.

     --II      Specify that ssppaammllooggdd is only to whitelist inbound SMTP connec‐
             tions.  By default ssppaammllooggdd will whitelist the source of inbound
             SMTP connections, and the target of outbound SMTP connections.

     --ii _i_n_t_e_r_f_a_c_e
             Specify a network interface on which packets must arrive.  The
             default is to watch for connections logged from all interfaces.

     --ll _p_f_l_o_g___i_n_t_e_r_f_a_c_e
             Specify a pflog(4) interface to listen for connection notifica‐
             tions.  The default is to watch for connections logged on
             “pflog0”.

     --WW _w_h_i_t_e_e_x_p
             Adjust the time for _w_h_i_t_e_e_x_p in hours.  The default is 864 hours
             (approximately 36 days); maximum is 2160 hours (approximately 90
             days).

     --YY _s_y_n_c_t_a_r_g_e_t
             Add a target to receive synchronisation messages; see
             _S_Y_N_C_H_R_O_N_I_S_A_T_I_O_N below.  This option can be specified multiple
             times.

     It is important to log any connections to and from the real MTA in order
     for ssppaammllooggdd to update the whitelist entries.  See spamd(8) for an exam‐
     ple ruleset for logging such connections.

     ssppaammllooggdd sends log messages to syslogd(8) using facility _d_a_e_m_o_n.
     ssppaammllooggdd will log each connection it sees at level LOG_DEBUG.

SSYYNNCCHHRROONNIISSAATTIIOONN
     ssppaammllooggdd supports realtime synchronisation of whitelist states by sending
     the information it updates to a number of spamd(8) daemons running on
     multiple machines.  To enable synchronisation, use the command line op‐
     tion --YY to specify the machines to which ssppaammllooggdd will send messages when
     it updates the state information.  For more information, see spamd(8).

